# Invisible ink: drying, browning and burning are different changes
# This lesson computes only the reviewed lemon-juice mark on paper. Its bounded
# brown appearance is not a general caramelisation or Maillard mechanism.
register lv2
# Wet control: heat alone cannot reveal a mark while water remains.
add v1 paper 2g
add v1 lemon_juice 2mL
heat v1 2kJ
look v1
# Dry the same mark first, then warm it. Browning does not ignite the paper.
evaporate v1 1
heat v1 2kJ
look v1
# Separate virtual burn control. Never ignite real paper for this activity.
new crucible
add v2 paper 2g
add v2 O2 0.5mol
ignite v2
look v2
